~ day2
Folly: Do you know why Brawny and Raincoat are suspicious of me?
Hermit: Yes.
Folly: Is it because of LORE
=> END!
~ night2
Folly: Hello [again].
Hermit: You know you aren't wanted here.
Folly: You don't like me?
Hermit: The others are the ones who don't like you. They glimpse what you are and it scares them.
Folly: Are you scared of me?
Hermit: ...No. I was in your place once. Perhaps we're here to stay, forever and ever, stuck in an endless loop of sameness.
=> END!
~ day3
Folly: I did something awful.
Hermit: What did you do?
Folly: MEMENTO TEST I threw a stone at Brawny and knocked him off the bridge!
Hermit: ...You haven't learned anything. Meet me tomorrow.
=> END!
~ night3
Folly: What do I do now? Everything I touch is falling apart!
Hermit: It is time you left. If you stay any longer, you will be entrenched here, trapped in the cobwebs of doubt, like me.
Folly: How do I leave?
Hermit: Seek forgiveness. But not from others. From yourself. Go home. I will help you tomorrow.
=> END!
